{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-29 01:57:42 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-ReadFileAudit] [Project: read_file_search_audit] Analyzed gap between read_file and grep/sed needs. CRITICAL FINDING: read_file search is SINGLE-FILE only with no multi-file capabilities. Claude Code has native Grep tool (ripgrep-based) with: recursive search, glob filters, type filters, context lines, output modes (content/files_with_matches/count), multiline support. Agents MUST use this Grep tool - no scribe wrapper needed. The real issue is POLICY not CAPABILITY. | confidence=1; reasoning={\"how\": \"Compared read_file capabilities to grep/rg features, identified that native Grep tool already exists and provides everything needed\", \"what\": \"Gap analysis complete: read_file lacks multi-file search, but Claude Code Grep tool already provides all needed features - agents just need to use it\", \"why\": \"User wants to eliminate sed/grep dependencies, but the real problem is PERMISSION not CAPABILITY\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_search_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-29T01:57:42.773115+00:00_ee56ab7a", "timestamp": "2026-01-29T01:57:42.773173+00:00"}
