{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-29 02:05:48 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-ReadFileAudit-R2] [Project: read_file_search_audit] Analyzed tool registration pattern. Tools use @app.tool() decorator pattern imported from server.py. Tool modules self-register on import. Simple pattern: (1) Import app from scribe_mcp.server, (2) Define async function with @app.tool() decorator, (3) Import tool module in tools/__init__.py to trigger registration. This makes adding new tools straightforward - just create new file with decorator and add import. | files_analyzed=2; pattern_identified=decorator_based_registration; reasoning={\"how\": \"Analyzed doctor.py as reference tool, confirmed pattern in __init__.py imports\", \"what\": \"Found simple decorator pattern - tool registration happens automatically on module import\", \"why\": \"Need to understand how to integrate new search tool into existing infrastructure\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_search_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-29T02:05:48.048768+00:00_1a14e37b", "timestamp": "2026-01-29T02:05:48.048851+00:00"}
