{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-29 02:06:33 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-ReadFileAudit-R2] [Project: read_file_search_audit] Analyzed read_file search implementation (lines 1604-1669). Uses Python's standard `re` module for regex and `difflib.SequenceMatcher` for fuzzy matching. Single-file only - opens file, reads line-by-line, maintains context buffer, matches pattern. Simple but effective. Performance: O(n) where n=lines in file. For multi-file search tool, can reuse this pattern but need: (1) File discovery mechanism, (2) Glob/type filtering, (3) Result aggregation across files, (4) Performance considerations for large codebases. | files_analyzed=3; libraries_used=[\"re\", \"difflib\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Analyzed _search_file function implementation, identified reusable patterns and extension points\", \"what\": \"Found simple Python-based search using stdlib - can be extended for multi-file use\", \"why\": \"Need to understand existing search patterns to inform new multi-file tool design\"}; search_implementation_location=read_file.py:1604-1669; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_search_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-29T02:06:33.999313+00:00_2352ea15", "timestamp": "2026-01-29T02:06:33.999445+00:00"}
