{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-29 02:24:52 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-ReadFileAudit-R3] [Project: read_file_search_audit] Research mission initialized: sed replacement design for MCP tools. Context: Previous research (R1 & R2) audited read_file gaps and designed new search tool to replace grep/rg. Now addressing the third piece: sed replacement for find-and-replace operations. Key question: Where should replace/edit capabilities live? (search tool, read_file, new edit_file tool, or hybrid approach). Starting comprehensive investigation of sed usage patterns and architecture options. | component=research; confidence=0.95; phase=initialization; reasoning={\"how\": \"Will investigate sed usage patterns, evaluate architecture options, analyze safety requirements, and recommend design that integrates with new search tool and read_file\", \"what\": \"Need to determine optimal architecture for sed replacement - which tool should own replace/edit capabilities\", \"why\": \"Building complete MCP toolkit to eliminate shell command dependency (grep/sed/rg) for agent file operations\"}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_search_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-29T02:24:52.373740+00:00_5f1cb6a4", "timestamp": "2026-01-29T02:24:52.373805+00:00"}
